# broiler-js cldr data pin 1
#
# The Unicode Common Locale Data Repository files the shared Intl data home's generator reads
# (Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation's Intl generator, work package SJL-9.2b of the shared JavaScript
# libraries programme), and the CLDR licence text. Broiler.VM's decision JSD-0082 (decisions D10 and
# D11) makes this pin a superset of Broiler.VM's src/tests/cldr/pins/cldr.pin: every line of that pin
# from `data` to its last `file` line is below, unchanged and in its order, and the `file` lines after
# them name this repository's extra files: main-data files from the same npm packages at the same
# version, and CLDR's common/main XML files for decision D21, from the CLDR repository at the tag
# Broiler.VM's common/main/root.xml came from.
#
# WHERE BROILER.VM'S FILES CAME FROM. They are byte-for-byte copies of Broiler.VM's src/tests/cldr/pins/
# at Broiler.VM 4cf9ca449fc96a1a5be810f6d0ca31c42b855c8f, the merge that carries its SJL-9 rules, kept
# at the same paths below this pin's directory. Broiler.VM's pin records how they were taken: the
# cldr-json packages from the npm registry, each tarball checked against the registry's sha512
# integrity stated below before it was unpacked; the collation files, common/main/root.xml and the
# licence from the CLDR repository at the tag release-48-2; each retrieved twice, on 2026-10-04 and
# 2026-10-05, into two directories found byte-identical. None of them was taken from a new retrieval
# for this copy. Each of its npm files was found byte-identical to its member of its package's tarball:
# a file from the packages the extension below reads, of the tarballs retrieved for it; a file from
# cldr-core or cldr-bcp47, which the extension does not read, of those two packages' tarballs,
# retrieved twice by Claude on 2026-10-26 from the same registry for this comparison alone, each pair
# byte-identical and each tarball's sha512 the integrity its json-integrity line states.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-26 FOR SJL-9.2b. Broiler.JS's embedding (decision D5; its list is
# ../locales/broiler-js.txt) reads the main data of every locale of its list that cldr-core's
# availableLocales.json names among its `full` locales. For each, it reads the files Broiler.VM's
# generator reads for de and en: numbers.json and currencies.json from cldr-numbers-full; units.json
# from cldr-units-full; listPatterns.json from cldr-misc-full; languages.json, territories.json,
# scripts.json, variants.json and localeDisplayNames.json from cldr-localenames-full; ca-generic.json,
# ca-gregorian.json, dateFields.json and timeZoneNames.json from cldr-dates-full; and from the
# cldr-cal-*-full packages the ca-*.json files of the calendars Broiler.VM's generator reads, which
# leave out ca-islamic-rgsa.json. A file Broiler.VM's lines already name is not named again. The
# tarballs of those packages were retrieved twice by Claude on 2026-10-26, from
# https://registry.npmjs.org/<package>/-/<package>-48.2.0.tgz, into two directories that `cmp` found
# byte-identical, and each was checked against the registry's sha512 integrity its json-integrity line
# below states before any file was read from it. The files are those tarballs' members, unmodified, at
# the same paths below json/<package>/ as Broiler.VM's. For a few locales cldr-localenames-full carries
# no languages.json, territories.json, scripts.json or variants.json; README.md beside this pin lists
# each such file, and the generator reads none for that locale. The repository owner directed on
# 2026-10-18 that the programme's recommended decisions be taken; no permission specific to this
# retrieval was given, and that is recorded here rather than implied.
#
# EXTENDED AGAIN 2026-10-26 FOR DECISION D21. Broiler.JS's number table carries each numbering
# system's own symbols for every locale of its list, through the locale's parent chain to root. A
# cldr-json numbers.json carries the symbols of a locale's default, native, traditional and finance
# systems only, so the generator reads the others from CLDR's XML: common/main/<locale>.xml for every
# main-data locale of the list but und, whose root.xml is Broiler.VM's entry, and for every locale on
# their parent chains below root (parentLocales.json's parent, or the tag less its last subtag), which
# adds en_001.xml. They were retrieved twice by Claude on 2026-10-26 from
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unicode-org/cldr/release-48-2/common/main/ (the repository-source
# line below) into two directories that `diff -r` found byte-identical, and root.xml, retrieved with
# them, equals Broiler.VM's entry. The files are unmodified; the same owner's direction applies.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. As in Broiler.VM's pin: `file <path relative to this directory> <bytes> <sha256>`.
# A supplemental JSON file states its CLDR major version, a package.json its package version and the
# UCA files their UCA version, which the generator's IntlCldrPin compares with the pinned ones; the
# main-data files, JSON and XML, the bcp47 files, the collation XML and the licence state none and are
# held by their hashes alone. The two CollationTest files are test-only input: no table is generated
# from them.

